//@version=6
// =====================================================================================================
//  NQ 9:15–9:30 NY OPENING RANGE BREAKOUT — with 5 selectable regime filters (A/B testing harness)
// =====================================================================================================
//
//  INSTRUMENT / CHART
//  - Built and defaulted for NQ1! (Nasdaq-100 E-mini futures, continuous) on the 15-minute chart.
//  - Symbol-agnostic: all logic is in PRICE POINTS, never dollars. MNQ1! (Micro) behaves identically;
//    only the dollar value per point differs (NQ = $20/point/contract, MNQ = $2/point/contract).
//    TradingView applies syminfo.pointvalue automatically, so no dollar value is hardcoded anywhere.
//  - Assumes 15-minute bars. Any timeframe <= 15 min also works (the range aggregates every bar that
//    opens inside the window, e.g. three 5-min bars). Timeframes > 15 min have no bar that opens inside
//    9:15–9:30, so no range is formed and the strategy will not trade (a warning shows in the info table).
//
//  TIMEZONE
//  - Every session / calendar call passes "America/New_York" explicitly. The chart/exchange timezone
//    (CME = America/Chicago) is never relied on.
//
//  OPENING RANGE
//  - Window = bars whose OPEN time is in [09:15, 09:30) NY. On 15m that is the single 9:15 bar
//    (spanning 9:15–9:30). Range high/low = highest high / lowest low of all bars in that window.
//  - The range locks when the last window bar closes (at 9:30). The first bar eligible to signal is the
//    first bar AFTER the window (the 9:30–9:45 bar on 15m). No signal can ever fire on a window bar.
//  - Range, "range set" flag and trade counter reset on the NY CALENDAR day change (midnight NY), not the
//    CME session change (18:00 NY). If a NY day has no window bars (holiday / closed), no trades occur.
//
//  ENTRIES (evaluated on bar close only — calc_on_every_tick = false)
//  - Long : close > rangeHigh AND close > open (bullish body closes above range)
//  - Short: close < rangeLow  AND close < open (bearish body closes below range)
//  - Must also pass the selected regime filter and the direction filter, be flat, and be under the
//    max-trades-per-day limit (default 1 = one trade per day regardless of outcome).
//  - FILL BEHAVIOR: Pine default (process_orders_on_close = false). The signal is computed at the close of
//    the breakout candle and the market order fills at the OPEN of the next bar. SL/TP levels are computed
//    from the breakout candle's CLOSE (the spec's "entry"), so realised R can differ slightly from planned R
//    when the next bar gaps. To fill exactly at the breakout close instead, change
//    process_orders_on_close to true in the strategy() call below.
//
//  STOP / TARGET (fixed at entry — no trailing, no breakeven)
//  - Long : SL = breakout candle low,  R = entry - SL, TP = entry + 0.5 * R
//  - Short: SL = breakout candle high, R = SL - entry, TP = entry - 0.5 * R
//  - Implemented with strategy.exit(stop=, limit=) tied to the matching entry ID.
//  - Note: if one bar touches both SL and TP, TradingView's broker emulator infers the intrabar path from
//    OHLC. Enable "Bar Magnifier" in Properties (if your plan supports it) for more accurate fills.
//
//  REGIME FILTERS ("Regime Filter" dropdown) — all evaluated on the breakout bar itself
//    None               : baseline, no gating
//    ADX Trend Strength : ADX >= threshold allows both sides                      (non-directional)
//    EMA Slope          : slope = (EMA - EMA[lb]) / lb; long slope > +min, short slope < -min (directional)
//    ATR Volatility     : ATR / SMA(ATR) >= min ratio allows both sides           (non-directional)
//    RSI Momentum       : long RSI >= longMin; short RSI <= shortMax              (directional)
//    Price vs VWAP      : long close > VWAP; short close < VWAP                   (directional)
//                         ta.vwap is anchored to the exchange session start (18:00 NY for CME futures).
//
//  POSITION SIZING — IMPORTANT
//  - strategy() is declared with initial_capital 10000 and 10% of equity per spec. However, one NQ
//    contract controls roughly price x $20 of notional (hundreds of thousands of dollars), so 10% of a
//    $10k account computes to a fraction of a contract, which TradingView rounds down to 0 -> NO TRADES.
//    The "Position Sizing" input therefore defaults to "Fixed Contracts" (1). Switch it to
//    "% of Equity (strategy default)" only if you also raise initial capital substantially.
//  - margin_long / margin_short are set to 0 (margin checks disabled) so the emulator doesn't force
//    margin-call liquidations on a small simulated account. Futures margin isn't modelled.
//  - Commission is $0.62 per contract per side (strategy.commission.cash_per_contract). Pine requires
//    strategy() arguments to be compile-time constants, so it cannot be driven by an input.* — adjust it
//    in the Strategy Tester: Settings (gear) > Properties > Commission.
//
//  HOW TO A/B TEST THE FILTERS
//  1. Add to NQ1!, 15-minute chart. Use as much history as your plan allows (Deep Backtesting if available).
//  2. Run the Strategy Tester once per "Regime Filter" option — start with "None" (baseline), then each of
//     the five filters, keeping every other input unchanged.
//  3. For each run record: Net P&L, Profit Factor, Win Rate (% profitable), Max Drawdown, Total Trades.
//  4. With a 0.5R target, break-even win rate before costs is 1 / (1 + 0.5) = ~66.7% (higher after
//     commission/slippage). Judge filters primarily on whether they cut false breakouts / chop — i.e.
//     raise Profit Factor and Win Rate and lower drawdown versus the baseline — NOT on raw trade count.
//     Beware filters that look good only because they leave a tiny sample of trades.
//  5. After choosing a filter, tune its parameters and validate on out-of-sample dates to avoid overfit.
// =====================================================================================================

strategy("NQ 9:15 ORB + Regime Filters",
     shorttitle             = "NQ ORB Regime",
     overlay                = true,
     initial_capital        = 10000,
     default_qty_type       = strategy.percent_of_equity,
     default_qty_value      = 10,
     commission_type        = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract,
     commission_value       = 0.62,
     calc_on_every_tick     = false,
     process_orders_on_close = false,
     pyramiding             = 0,
     margin_long            = 0,
     margin_short           = 0)

// =====================================================================================================
// CONSTANTS
// =====================================================================================================
const string NY = "America/New_York"   // single source of truth for all session/calendar calls

const string F_NONE = "None"
const string F_ADX  = "ADX Trend Strength"
const string F_EMA  = "EMA Slope"
const string F_ATR  = "ATR Volatility"
const string F_RSI  = "RSI Momentum"
const string F_VWAP = "Price vs VWAP"

const string D_BOTH  = "Both"
const string D_LONG  = "Long Only"
const string D_SHORT = "Short Only"

const string SZ_FIXED = "Fixed Contracts"
const string SZ_PCT   = "% of Equity (strategy default)"

// =====================================================================================================
// INPUTS
// =====================================================================================================
const string G_RANGE = "Opening Range"
string rangeSess = input.session("0915-0930", "Range Window (NY time)", group = G_RANGE,
     tooltip = "Bars whose open time falls in this window (New York time, Mon–Fri) build the range. Default 09:15–09:30. On 15m this is the single 9:15 bar.")
float  tpMultR   = input.float(0.5, "Take Profit (x R)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = G_RANGE,
     tooltip = "Target distance as a multiple of risk R. Spec default 0.5.")

const string G_FILTER = "Regime Filter"
string regimeFilter = input.string(F_NONE, "Regime Filter", options = [F_NONE, F_ADX, F_EMA, F_ATR, F_RSI, F_VWAP], group = G_FILTER,
     tooltip = "Select one filter per backtest run. 'None' = baseline with no gating.")
bool   showFilterSeries = input.bool(true, "Plot active filter series (EMA / VWAP on chart)", group = G_FILTER)

const string G_ADX = "1) ADX Trend Strength"
int    adxLen       = input.int(14, "ADX Length (DI + smoothing)", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = G_ADX)
float  adxThreshold = input.float(25.0, "ADX Threshold (>=)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 0.5, group = G_ADX)

const string G_EMA = "2) EMA Slope"
int    emaLen      = input.int(50, "EMA Length", minval = 1, maxval = 500, group = G_EMA)
int    emaSlopeLb  = input.int(5, "Slope Lookback (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = G_EMA)
float  emaMinSlope = input.float(0.0, "Min |Slope| (points per bar)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = G_EMA,
     tooltip = "Long requires slope > +value; short requires slope < -value.")

const string G_ATR = "3) ATR Volatility Expansion"
int    atrLen      = input.int(14, "ATR Length", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = G_ATR)
int    atrSmaLen   = input.int(50, "ATR SMA Length", minval = 1, maxval = 500, group = G_ATR)
float  atrMinRatio = input.float(1.2, "Min ATR / SMA(ATR) Ratio", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.05, group = G_ATR)

const string G_RSI = "4) RSI Momentum"
int    rsiLen      = input.int(14, "RSI Length", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = G_RSI)
float  rsiLongMin  = input.float(50.0, "Long: RSI >=", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 0.5, group = G_RSI)
float  rsiShortMax = input.float(50.0, "Short: RSI <=", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 0.5, group = G_RSI)

// 5) Price vs VWAP has no parameters (session-anchored ta.vwap on hlc3).

const string G_EXEC = "Execution / Sizing"
string sizingMode = input.string(SZ_FIXED, "Position Sizing", options = [SZ_FIXED, SZ_PCT], group = G_EXEC,
     tooltip = "10% of a $10k account is far less than one NQ contract and rounds to 0 (no trades). Fixed Contracts is the practical default.")
int    fixedQty   = input.int(1, "Fixed Contracts", minval = 1, maxval = 1000, group = G_EXEC)

const string G_OPT = "Optional Enhancements"
bool   useEod      = input.bool(false, "End-of-Day Flatten", group = G_OPT, inline = "eod",
     tooltip = "Close any open position on the first bar that CLOSES at/after this NY time (fills at the next bar's open). Also blocks new entries after this time. On 15m, 15:45 exits at ~15:45.")
int    eodHour     = input.int(15, "Hr", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = G_OPT, inline = "eod")
int    eodMinute   = input.int(45, "Min", minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = G_OPT, inline = "eod")
bool   useCutoff   = input.bool(false, "Last Entry Time", group = G_OPT, inline = "cut",
     tooltip = "No new entries on bars that close after this NY time. Off = entries allowed any time after the range locks until the NY day ends.")
int    cutHour     = input.int(12, "Hr", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = G_OPT, inline = "cut")
int    cutMinute   = input.int(0, "Min", minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = G_OPT, inline = "cut")
int    maxTradesPerDay = input.int(1, "Max Trades Per Day", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = G_OPT,
     tooltip = "Spec default 1: after the first entry (win or lose) no more entries that NY day.")
string dirFilter   = input.string(D_BOTH, "Signal Direction", options = [D_BOTH, D_LONG, D_SHORT], group = G_OPT)
bool   showTable   = input.bool(true, "Show Info Table", group = G_OPT)

// =====================================================================================================
// NY TIME HELPERS
// =====================================================================================================
// NY calendar-day key (YYYYMMDD). Changes at midnight New York, independent of the CME session break.
int  nyDayKey = year(time, NY) * 10000 + month(time, NY) * 100 + dayofmonth(time, NY)
bool newNyDay = bar_index == 0 or nyDayKey != nz(nyDayKey[1])

// Bar CLOSE time in NY minutes-of-day (used for EOD flatten and entry cutoff).
int  closeMinNy = hour(time_close, NY) * 60 + minute(time_close, NY)

// Is this bar inside the opening-range window? NY timezone passed explicitly; Mon–Fri only.
bool inRangeWindow = not na(time(timeframe.period, rangeSess + ":23456", NY))

// =====================================================================================================
// RANGE CAPTURE
// =====================================================================================================
var float rangeHigh       = na
var float rangeLow        = na
var bool  rangeHasData    = false   // at least one window bar seen today
var bool  rangeSet        = false   // range locked (window finished) for today
var int   tradesToday     = 0
var bool  tradeTakenToday = false

// Daily reset on NY calendar day change (must run BEFORE capture so a new day starts clean).
if newNyDay
    rangeHigh       := na
    rangeLow        := na
    rangeHasData    := false
    rangeSet        := false
    tradesToday     := 0
    tradeTakenToday := false

// Aggregate every bar that opens inside the window (works for 1/3/5/15-min charts alike).
if inRangeWindow and not rangeSet
    rangeHigh    := na(rangeHigh) ? high : math.max(rangeHigh, high)
    rangeLow     := na(rangeLow)  ? low  : math.min(rangeLow, low)
    rangeHasData := true

// Lock the range on the first bar AFTER the window. A day with no window bars never locks -> no trades.
if not rangeSet and not inRangeWindow and inRangeWindow[1] and rangeHasData
    rangeSet := true

// =====================================================================================================
// REGIME FILTER SERIES (computed every bar at global scope for consistent history)
// =====================================================================================================
[diPlus, diMinus, adxVal] = ta.dmi(adxLen, adxLen)

float emaVal   = ta.ema(close, emaLen)
float emaSlope = (emaVal - emaVal[emaSlopeLb]) / emaSlopeLb

float atrVal   = ta.atr(atrLen)
float atrSma   = ta.sma(atrVal, atrSmaLen)
float atrRatio = atrSma > 0 ? atrVal / atrSma : na

float rsiVal   = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)

float vwapVal  = ta.vwap(hlc3)   // session-anchored VWAP

// =====================================================================================================
// REGIME GATES (evaluated on the same bar as the breakout; na values never pass)
// =====================================================================================================
bool regimeLongOk  = true
bool regimeShortOk = true

if regimeFilter == F_ADX
    bool ok = not na(adxVal) and adxVal >= adxThreshold
    regimeLongOk  := ok
    regimeShortOk := ok
else if regimeFilter == F_EMA
    regimeLongOk  := not na(emaSlope) and emaSlope >  emaMinSlope
    regimeShortOk := not na(emaSlope) and emaSlope < -emaMinSlope
else if regimeFilter == F_ATR
    bool ok = not na(atrRatio) and atrRatio >= atrMinRatio
    regimeLongOk  := ok
    regimeShortOk := ok
else if regimeFilter == F_RSI
    regimeLongOk  := not na(rsiVal) and rsiVal >= rsiLongMin
    regimeShortOk := not na(rsiVal) and rsiVal <= rsiShortMax
else if regimeFilter == F_VWAP
    regimeLongOk  := not na(vwapVal) and close > vwapVal
    regimeShortOk := not na(vwapVal) and close < vwapVal

// =====================================================================================================
// SIGNAL GENERATION
// =====================================================================================================
bool allowLongDir  = dirFilter != D_SHORT
bool allowShortDir = dirFilter != D_LONG

bool eodReached   = useEod    and closeMinNy >= eodHour * 60 + eodMinute
bool pastCutoff   = useCutoff and closeMinNy >  cutHour * 60 + cutMinute

// Entry eligibility: range locked, not a range-defining bar, na guard, daily limit, flat, time limits.
bool canEnter = rangeSet
     and not inRangeWindow
     and not na(rangeHigh) and not na(rangeLow)
     and tradesToday < maxTradesPerDay
     and strategy.position_size == 0
     and not eodReached
     and not pastCutoff

bool longBreak  = close > rangeHigh and close > open   // bullish body close above range
bool shortBreak = close < rangeLow  and close < open   // bearish body close below range

bool longSignal  = canEnter and longBreak  and regimeLongOk  and allowLongDir
bool shortSignal = canEnter and shortBreak and regimeShortOk and allowShortDir

// =====================================================================================================
// EXECUTION
// =====================================================================================================
float orderQty = sizingMode == SZ_FIXED ? float(fixedQty) : na   // na -> use strategy() default sizing

var float slLevel = na
var float tpLevel = na

if longSignal
    float entryRef = close
    float stopPx   = low
    float riskR    = entryRef - stopPx           // > 0 guaranteed: bullish bar => low <= open < close
    slLevel := stopPx
    tpLevel := entryRef + tpMultR * riskR
    strategy.entry("ORB Long", strategy.long, qty = orderQty)
    strategy.exit("ORB Long Exit", from_entry = "ORB Long", stop = slLevel, limit = tpLevel,
         comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP")
    tradesToday     += 1
    tradeTakenToday := true

if shortSignal
    float entryRef = close
    float stopPx   = high
    float riskR    = stopPx - entryRef           // > 0 guaranteed: bearish bar => high >= open > close
    slLevel := stopPx
    tpLevel := entryRef - tpMultR * riskR
    strategy.entry("ORB Short", strategy.short, qty = orderQty)
    strategy.exit("ORB Short Exit", from_entry = "ORB Short", stop = slLevel, limit = tpLevel,
         comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP")
    tradesToday     += 1
    tradeTakenToday := true

// Optional end-of-day flatten (market close at next bar open).
if eodReached and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all(comment = "EOD Flatten")

// =====================================================================================================
// VISUALIZATION
// =====================================================================================================
// Opening range lines: drawn from the lock bar to the end of the NY day, broken between days.
plot(rangeSet ? rangeHigh : na, "Range High", color.new(color.green, 0), 2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(rangeSet ? rangeLow  : na, "Range Low",  color.new(color.red, 0),   2, plot.style_linebr)

// Shade the range window.
bgcolor(inRangeWindow ? color.new(color.blue, 85) : na, title = "Range Window")

// Active SL/TP while in a position.
bool inPos = strategy.position_size != 0
plot(inPos ? slLevel : na, "Stop Loss",   color.new(color.orange, 0), 1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(inPos ? tpLevel : na, "Take Profit", color.new(color.aqua, 0),   1, plot.style_linebr)

// Active filter series on price (EMA / VWAP); oscillator values go to the Data Window only.
plot(showFilterSeries and regimeFilter == F_EMA  ? emaVal  : na, "EMA (filter)",  color.new(color.yellow, 0), 2)
plot(showFilterSeries and regimeFilter == F_VWAP ? vwapVal : na, "VWAP (filter)", color.new(color.fuchsia, 0), 2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(regimeFilter == F_ADX ? adxVal   : na, "ADX (filter)",       display = display.data_window)
plot(regimeFilter == F_EMA ? emaSlope : na, "EMA Slope (filter)", display = display.data_window)
plot(regimeFilter == F_ATR ? atrRatio : na, "ATR Ratio (filter)", display = display.data_window)
plot(regimeFilter == F_RSI ? rsiVal   : na, "RSI (filter)",       display = display.data_window)

// Info table (last bar only).
var table info = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 7, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 80),
     border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60), border_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 40), frame_width = 1)

if showTable and barstate.islast
    string filterVal = regimeFilter == F_ADX  ? "ADX " + str.tostring(adxVal, "#.##") :
                       regimeFilter == F_EMA  ? "Slope " + str.tostring(emaSlope, "#.###") :
                       regimeFilter == F_ATR  ? "Ratio " + str.tostring(atrRatio, "#.###") :
                       regimeFilter == F_RSI  ? "RSI " + str.tostring(rsiVal, "#.##") :
                       regimeFilter == F_VWAP ? "VWAP " + str.tostring(vwapVal, format.mintick) : "—"
    bool tfOk = timeframe.in_seconds() <= 900
    table.cell(info, 0, 0, "Filter",      text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 1, 0, regimeFilter,  text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 0, 1, "Filter value", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 1, 1, filterVal,     text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 0, 2, "Range High",  text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 1, 2, na(rangeHigh) ? "—" : str.tostring(rangeHigh, format.mintick), text_color = color.green, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 0, 3, "Range Low",   text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 1, 3, na(rangeLow) ? "—" : str.tostring(rangeLow, format.mintick), text_color = color.red, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 0, 4, "Range locked", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 1, 4, rangeSet ? "Yes" : "No", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 0, 5, "Trades today", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 1, 5, str.tostring(tradesToday) + " / " + str.tostring(maxTradesPerDay), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 0, 6, "Timeframe",   text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(info, 1, 6, tfOk ? timeframe.period + " OK" : timeframe.period + " — use <= 15m", text_color = tfOk ? color.white : color.orange, text_size = size.small)
